    "text_result": "Fixed. I removed the `src/mongo/db/repl/initial_sync/initial_syncer.cpp` entry from `auto_merged` (it's listed under `important_files_modified`, not `auto_merged.files`) and updated the `review_notes` to no longer reference it. The response now describes only the 30 files in `merge_context.auto_merged.files`, each backed by the actual `diff base \u2192 merge commit` diff I read.",
    "response": {
      "summary": "This merge pulls in upstream MongoDB changes since the fork diverged (base b22243acf40 -> merge commit ff54e20bb1). The main themes are: (1) migrating the Bazel `dependency` helper from the removed `@poetry//:dependencies.bzl` to the new `//bazel/uv:defs.bzl`; (2) making the server-side JavaScript engine conditional on the target platform so ppc64le builds link `scripting_none`, with matching test guards that skip scripting/mapReduce commands where JS is unavailable; (3) splitting the `metrics_policy_manager` Bazel target into mongod- and mongos-specific variants; (4) a large amount of mechanical IWYU include reordering across several C++ files (own header first, then std, then third-party, with `IWYU pragma: no_include` lines moved to the bottom); (5) tightening WiredTiger table-creation option validation; (6) new auth test coverage for forged `runtimeConstants.userRoles` and `$listSessions` `$_internalPredicate`; and a few smaller server behavior tweaks. The MODULE.bazel.lock is regenerated to match the new dependency graph.",
      "auto_merged": {
        ".bazelrc": "Adds a single blank line before the `venvs_site_packages=no` comment/setting block. No functional change.",
