        "BUILD.bazel": "Replaces the `load(\"@poetry//:dependencies.bzl\", \"dependency\")` with `load(\"//bazel/uv:defs.bzl\", \"dependency\")`, moving the `dependency` helper from the old poetry rules to the new uv-based defs.",
        "MODULE.bazel.lock": "Regenerated Bazel module lock file reflecting updated/added registry dependencies (e.g. bazel_features 1.43.0, bazel_lib 3.1.0, package_metadata 0.0.7, newer rules_cc versions) and removed older entries. This is a machine-generated lock, not a hand-authored change; the conflict was resolved and the file regenerated.",
        "bazel/config/BUILD.bazel": "Adds a new `selects.config_setting_group` named `server_js_engine_allowed` that matches both `:server_js_enabled` and `:not_ppc`. This ensures a server-side JS engine is only linked when server_js is enabled AND the target is not ppc64le, so any ppc64le build links scripting_none regardless of the server_js flag.",
        "bazel/resmoke/resmoke.bzl": "Reworks how the resmoke config generator's Python import paths are computed. Adds loads for `py_exec_import_paths` (from //bazel/config:py_action_env), `py_test`, and `PyInfo`, and replaces the manual `$(BINDIR)/external/...` PyInfo.imports loop with a call to `py_exec_import_paths(ctx, [ctx.attr.generator])`. The `generator` attribute is now declared with `cfg = \"exec\"` so the config-generation action runs the exec-platform interpreter with exec-config wheels.",
        "buildscripts/resmokelib/core/programs.py": "Adds a `remove_set_parameter_if_before_version` call that strips the `migrationRecipientPITHistoryToPreserveInSecs` set parameter for binary versions before 9.0.0.",
        "buildscripts/resmokelib/testing/fixtures/standalone.py": "Defaults the `migrationRecipientPITHistoryToPreserveInSecs` suite set parameter to 1 when not already specified, with a comment explaining that this controls the point-in-time history window preserved by chunk migrations in tests (mirroring minSnapshotHistoryWindowInSeconds in production).",
        "jstests/auth/lib/commands_lib.js": "Adds an `elevatedUserRolesRuntimeConstants` fixture and new negative test cases verifying that a forged `runtimeConstants.userRoles` is rejected for external clients on find/update/delete/findAndModify (sharded and non-sharded)/aggregate (with the appropriate mongod vs mongos error codes). Adds `$listSessions` `$_internalPredicate` auth tests requiring the `internal` (and, with allUsers:true, `listSessions`) cluster privileges. Adds an `isServerSideJavaScriptEnabled(conn)` helper (detects a scripting_none build via absence of the `js` sub-document in the `features` command) and gates the mapReduce_readonly/mapReduce_write test cases behind `skipTest` when server-side JS is unavailable.",
        "jstests/core/catalog/views/views_all_commands.js": "Imports `isServerSideJavaScriptEnabled` and adds a `skipNoScripting: true` flag to the mapReduce view command test; the test loop now skips such commands when server-side JS is unavailable on the build.",
